-- title:
--   RH height 14–100 — theta coefficient data, part C
-- statement:
--   Rounded integer Taylor coefficients and error radii for the theta exponential jets in the height-14–100 certificate. This part contains 14 active panel/theta-term records, ordered as [(7, 0), (7, 1), (7, 2), (8, 0), (8, 1), (8, 2), (9, 0), (9, 1), (10, 0), (10, 1), (11, 0), (12, 0), (13, 0), (14, 0)]. Each record has 184 centers and 184 radii at decimal scale 10^310. These are proposed finite data, not assumed bounds: the main height-block proof checks every enclosure, recurrence residual, rounding condition and carry bound. The theta/Mellin foundations retain attribution to Gabewhigham; the finite-certificate construction is from sometik179’s October 3, 2026 proof source.
--
--   **Port note.** This is a port, to the Mathlib `777aaa6` / Lean v4.29.0-rc3 environment of the Riemann Hypothesis mission tree, of the definition `TaoFivePrimes_RH14To100ThetaDataC` (id `a68551ad-5553-45bc-b922-ffddbd5e8f1b`, env `0df444a`, published by @raresbuhai). Changes: the single literal list is split into one named definition per entry (Lean v4.29.0-rc3 overflows its stack elaborating the original 8000-element literal); the resulting list value is identical.
-- source:
